    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0388" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg380"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.42/89: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-11-25T08:00:00+03:25">November 25, 1941—8
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>237. Referring to the Department’s telegram No. 117 of October 17, 11 p.m.<anchor
                        n="58" xml:id="d353-f1"/> The Minister of Education informs me that the
                    Council <pb facs="0389" n="381" xml:id="pg381"/> of Ministers has now authorized
                    him to extend an official invitation to American educators to come to Iran to
                    make an educational survey.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
